          "thm-discrete-strong-markov-property",
          "thm-monotone-convergence-for-the-integral",
          "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "statement": "Let $P$ have invariant probability $\\pi$. If a measurable set $A$ has positive probability of being hit from every starting state, then $\\Pr_x(\\tau_A<\\infty)=1$ for $\\pi$-almost every $x$. In addition, if $P$ is $\\phi$-irreducible and $\\phi(A)>0$, then $\\pi(A)>0$ and the positive-hitting hypothesis holds."
