      {
        "id": "lem-geometric-drift-minorization-reduces-to-bounded-small-set",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Geometric drift yields a bounded small set and bivariate drift",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-general-state-aperiodic-markov-chain",
          "def-invariant-and-stationary-distribution-for-a-markov-kernel",
          "def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel",
          "def-petite-set-for-markov-kernel",
          "def-phi-irreducible-chain",
          "def-small-set-minorization-and-drift",
          "lem-aperiodic-minorization-times-are-cofinite",
          "lem-aperiodic-petite-set-with-accessible-small-set-is-small",
          "lem-bivariate-drift-minorization-coupling-rate",
          "lem-drift-sublevel-union-is-petite",
          "lem-invariant-law-positive-set-and-almost-sure-hitting"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 4,
        "statement": "Let $P$ be countably generated, $\\phi$-irreducible and aperiodic with invariant probability $\\pi$. Suppose $C$ is $(m,\\epsilon,\\nu)$-small with $\\phi(C)>0$ and $PV\\le\\lambda V+b1_C$ for finite $V\\ge1$, $0<\\lambda<1$. Then there are $\\lambda'\\in(\\lambda,1)$ and a $\\phi$-positive small set $C_0\\subseteq C$ with $\\sup_{C_0}V<\\infty$ and $PV\\le\\lambda'V+b1_{C_0}$ pointwise. Moreover there are a bounded-$V$ small set $D$, a time $L$, a minorizing probability $\\nu'$, and $a<1$ such that for $Q=P^L$ and $h(x,y)=(V(x)+V(y))/2$,\n$$Q\\otimes Q\\,h\\le ah\\quad\\text{off }D^2.$$\nIf $Q(x,\\cdot)\\ge\\epsilon_D\\nu'$ on $D$, the residual laws $R_x=(Q(x,\\cdot)-\\epsilon_D\\nu')/(1-\\epsilon_D)$ have $\\sup_{x,y\\in D}R_x\\otimes R_y(h)<\\infty$ when $\\epsilon_D<1$; for $\\epsilon_D=1$ no residual branch is needed."
      },
