      {
        "id": "thm-geometric-ergodicity-under-drift-and-minorization",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Geometric ergodicity under drift and small-set minorization",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-general-state-aperiodic-markov-chain",
          "def-invariant-and-stationary-distribution-for-a-markov-kernel",
          "def-phi-irreducible-chain",
          "def-small-set-minorization-and-drift",
          "def-total-variation-distance-for-probability-laws",
          "def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel",
          "cor-finite-nonnegative-integral-implies-finite-almost-everywhere",
          "lem-invariant-law-positive-set-and-almost-sure-hitting",
          "lem-total-variation-coupling-and-kernel-contraction",
          "lem-bivariate-drift-minorization-coupling-rate",
          "lem-geometric-drift-minorization-reduces-to-bounded-small-set",
          "lem-invariant-law-integrates-bounded-set-drift"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "statement": "Let $P$ be countably generated, $\\phi$-irreducible and aperiodic with invariant probability $\\pi$. Suppose a $\\phi$-positive small set $C$ and finite-valued $V\\ge1$ satisfy $PV\\le\\lambda V+b1_C$ for $0<\\lambda<1$. Then there are $M<\\infty$ and $0<r<1$ such that\n$$\\|P^n(x,\\cdot)-\\pi\\|_{\\rm TV}\\le M V(x)r^n\\quad(x\\in\\mathsf X,\\ n\\ge0).$$\nThis is geometric ergodicity with a $V$-weighted bound.\n\nUnder the same kernel, $\\phi$-positive small-set and drift-constant hypotheses, the result also holds if $V:\\mathsf X\\to[1,+\\infty]$ is measurable and finite $\\pi$-almost everywhere, with the drift inequality holding pointwise in the extended sense. Then $E=\\{V<\\infty\\}$ is measurable, absorbing and of full $\\pi$-measure, and the displayed bound holds for every $x\\in E$. Thus extended certificates give the common geometric rate for $\\pi$-almost every start, while globally finite certificates give it for every start."
      }
